+#
+# mido (Redmi Note 4 Snapdragon, MSM8953): the sweet master verbatim.
+#
+# Every option here is Qualcomm-generic, not board-specific, and this file being
+# present at all is what matters: SETUP/config/doconf is invoked with
+# -soc $(CURRENT_MACHINE_CONFIG_LC) and each component's conf/Makefile only pulls
+# MASTER.arm64.<machine> in when that file exists, so without it the build falls
+# back to Apple's stock arm64 master. That one expects the low-level symbols to
+# come from the KDK's closed lib<SOC>.os.<CONFIG>.a, and here that shows up as
+# 264 undefined symbols at link time (CleanPoC_Dcache, InvalidatePoU_Icache,
+# Idle_context, ResetHandlerData, __start, __bcopyin, ...) because nothing
+# compiled osfmk/arm64/{caches_asm,start,locore,cswitch}.s - those file entries
+# are tagged `nos_arm_asm`, which is an option that has to be turned on, not a
+# name saying "no assembly".
+#
+# polaris is compiled as a sweet variant anyway (-DARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET, see
+# MACHINE_FLAGS_ARM64_MIDO), so sharing one master is consistent with that.
+#
+# Unlike sweet's own file this one is created last, from the fully patched
+# MASTER.arm64.sweet, so it already carries every later addition: mockfs ramdisk
+# root, bindfs and the stubbed ext resolver.
